@page "/docs/extensions/maps"

<Seo Canonical="/docs/extensions/maps" Title="Blazorise Maps component" Description="Learn how to use the Blazorise Maps component to display interactive maps, markers, popups, shapes, and location data in Blazor applications." />

<DocsPageTitle Path="Extensions/Maps" AddedVersion="2.1" AddedDate="2026-04-14">
    Blazorise Maps component
</DocsPageTitle>

<DocsPageLead>
    Display interactive maps with tile layers, markers, and geographic shapes.
</DocsPageLead>

<DocsPageParagraph>
    The Maps extension follows the same abstraction principles as the rest of Blazorise: applications work with Blazorise components and models instead of being coupled directly to a specific map provider.
</DocsPageParagraph>

<DocsPageParagraph>
    The first implementation uses Leaflet internally while keeping the public component model provider-neutral. This allows additional map providers to be supported over time without changing how applications compose maps, layers, markers, and shapes.
</DocsPageParagraph>

<DocsPageParagraph>
    To use the <Code>Map</Code> component, install the <Code>Blazorise.Maps</Code> package first.
</DocsPageParagraph>

<DocsPageSectionTitle>
    Structure
</DocsPageSectionTitle>

<DocsPageParagraph>
    A <Code>Map</Code> contains the layers and features to display. Add the tile source, markers, and shapes your map needs.
</DocsPageParagraph>

<DocsAnatomy Label="Map component anatomy">
    <DocsAnatomyRegion Label="Map" Description="Hosts the map, manages its view, and coordinates child layers.">
        <DocsAnatomyRegion Label="MapTileLayer" Description="Defines the raster tile source, attribution, zoom range, and tile options." />
        <DocsAnatomyRegion Label="MapMarker" Description="Displays one location with optional text, icon, popup, and interaction." />
        <DocsAnatomyRegion Label="MapMarkerLayer" Description="Creates markers from a collection using selectors for location and behavior." />
        <DocsAnatomyRegion Label="MapCircle" Description="Draws a circular area from a center coordinate and radius." />
        <DocsAnatomyRegion Label="MapPolyline" Description="Draws a route or path through coordinates." />
        <DocsAnatomyRegion Label="MapPolygon" Description="Draws closed areas or boundaries with optional stroke and fill." />
    </DocsAnatomyRegion>
</DocsAnatomy>

<DocsPageParagraph>
    All layer components derive from <Code>MapLayer</Code>, which provides shared visibility, opacity, ordering, interaction, and registration behavior.
</DocsPageParagraph>

